02.pdf","committee":"West Suffolk Council Constitution","date":"08/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"CAB-WS-26-021-Appendix-2-Evaluation-Framework","url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s58370/cab-ws-26-021-appendix-2-evaluation-framework.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"19/05/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-06","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; *RESERVE DATE*","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-17","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; *RESERVE DATE*","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-16","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-21","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-23","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Overall borrowing expected to increase over the year despite early external debt repayment","lead":"Signals ongoing cash management pressure; the substantial internal borrowing (\u00a360.6m) and expected overall increase warrant monitoring for potential future PWLB drawdown","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"CAB-WS-26-039-Recs-from-PASC-Treasury-Management-Report-June-2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59409/59409.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Interest income significantly outperformed budget in the first quarter","lead":"Material variance to budget indicates either stronger cash generation or more favorable investment rates than forecast; relevant to full-year financial outturn","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"CAB-WS-26-039-Recs-from-PASC-Treasury-Management-Report-June-2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59409/59409.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Capital Projects Financing Reserve of \u00a39.3m provides thin cover against refinancing cost shock","lead":"The reserve is modest relative to the \u00a357.96m internal borrowing that will eventually require external refinancing. If capital acceleration occurs or rates rise further, the reserve could deplete quickly, leaving no buffer for cost overruns or additional\u2026","iso":"2026-07-23","paper_title":"FRS-WS-26-003-Annual-Treasury-Management-and-Financial-Resilience-Report-2025-to-2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59049/59049.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"CAB-WS-26-039-Recs-from-PASC-Treasury-Management-Report-June-2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59409/59409.pdf","headline":"Overall borrowing expected to increase over the year despite early external debt repayment","detail":"External borrowing decreased by \u00a3125,000 in the first quarter to \u00a38.875m, following the recent \u00a310m PWLB 40-year loan. However, internal borrowing stands at \u00a360.6m and overall borrowing is forecast to increase over the full financial year.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Signals ongoing cash management pressure; the substantial internal borrowing (\u00a360.6m) and expected overall increase warrant monitoring for potential future PWLB drawdown","figures":"External borrowing \u00a38,875,000 (down \u00a3125,000); internal borrowing \u00a360,634,266","quote":"Overall borrowing (total of both external and internal) is expected to increase over the full financial year.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"CAB-WS-26-039-Recs-from-PASC-Treasury-Management-Report-June-2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59409/59409.pdf","headline":"Interest income significantly outperformed budget in the first quarter","detail":"The council achieved \u00a3341,437 in interest income in the first three months of 2026/27, more than double the budgeted figure of \u00a3157,500 for the same period. This represents strong cash management during a period of elevated interest rates.","category":"income","matters":"Material variance to budget indicates either stronger cash generation or more favorable investment rates than forecast; relevant to full-year financial outturn","figures":"\u00a3341,437 achieved vs \u00a3157,500 budgeted (Q1 2026/27)","quote":"Interest achieved in the first three months of the financial year amounted to \u00a3341,437 against a budget for the period of \u00a3157,500.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-23","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"FRS-WS-26-003-Annual-Treasury-Management-and-Financial-Resilience-Report-2025-to-2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59049/59049.pdf","headline":"Capital Projects Financing Reserve of \u00a39.3m provides thin cover against refinancing cost shock","detail":"The council has earmarked \u00a39.3m in the Capital Projects Financing Reserve to mitigate adverse interest rate and investment return fluctuations, and specifically to fund additional borrowing costs from PWLB rates higher than assumed in project business cases. The difference between current PWLB rates (6.30%) and budgeted rates creates an annual cost gap that would consume the reserve within ~4.8 years.","category":"reserves","matters":"The reserve is modest relative to the \u00a357.96m internal borrowing that will eventually require external refinancing. If capital acceleration occurs or rates rise further, the reserve could deplete quickly, leaving no buffer for cost overruns or additional rate rises.","figures":"Capital Projects Financing Reserve \u00a39,296,075. Implied annual refinancing cost gap at current rates ~\u00a31.95m (\u00a33,820,756 potential future interest less \u00a31,865,950 budgeted).","quote":"The Council has an earmarked revenue reserve to mitigate against possible adverse fluctuations in the returns received from the council's investments and external borrowing costs, called the Capital Projects Financing Reserve. The balance in this reserve as at 31 March 2026 was \u00a39,296,075.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-23","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"FRS-WS-26-003-Annual-Treasury-Management-and-Financial-Resilience-Report-2025-to-2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59049/59049.pdf","headline":"Internal borrowing \u00a357.96m and rising; refinancing to external at 6.30% would add \u00a31.95m annual interest cost","detail":"West Suffolk's internal borrowing increased by \u00a38.27m to \u00a357.96m during 2025-26, while external borrowing fell from \u00a39.25m to \u00a39m. The council is funding its capital requirement from cash reserves (now \u00a327.8m, above the \u00a320m forecast) rather than external borrowing. Converting all internal borrowing to 40-year PWLB Certainty Rate borrowing at 6.30% would incur annual interest of \u00a33.82m, versus the budgeted \u00a31.87m\u2014an annual gap of \u00a31.95m.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Internal borrowing relies on available cash; once capital projects spend down reserves, external refinancing becomes mandatory. The rate jump from 1.84% existing to 6.30% new creates a cliff of unexpected additional borrowing costs. This affects debt affordability and could pressure the revenue budget once capital is deployed.","figures":"Internal borrowing \u00a357,963,592 (up from \u00a349,688,598). Cash held \u00a327,810,000 vs forecast \u00a320,000,000. At 6.30% PWLB Certainty Rate, annual interest on internal borrowing would be \u00a33,820,756 vs budgeted \u00a31,865,950.","quote":"if we were to transfer all of that internal borrowing to a 40 year PWLB loan using the 6.30 percent Certainty Rate, the Council would incur an initial annual interest payable cost of \u00a33,820,756 (including our current external borrowing). This compares to our interest payable budget for 2025 to 2026 of \u00a31,865,950.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-23","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"FRS-WS-26-003-Annual-Treasury-Management-and-Financial-Resilience-Report-2025-to-2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59049/59049.pdf","headline":"Capital programme \u00a344.9m underspent, with borrowing requirement only 60% of budget","detail":"The council budgeted a \u00a3111.9m borrowing requirement to fund capital projects in 2025-26, but actual borrowing requirement at year-end was \u00a366.96m\u2014a \u00a344.9m shortfall (40%). This reflects delayed capital expenditure across major projects including Mildenhall Hub, West Suffolk Operational Hub, Bury Leisure Centre Improvement, and the Net Zero Community Energy Plan. The council's Capital Financing Requirement increased by \u00a38.02m, but was entirely absorbed by internal borrowing from cash reserves rather than external borrowing.","category":"capital","matters":"Capital programme delays create delivery risk on strategic projects and defer revenue cost recognition. More importantly, when projects accelerate and cash depletes, the council will need to externally borrow at PWLB Certainty Rates now at 6.30% for 40-year terms\u2014342 basis points above the 1.84% rate on existing debt.","figures":"Budgeted capital borrowing requirement \u00a3111,859,015; actual \u00a366,963,592 (variance \u00a344,895,423, 40% underspent).","quote":"Borrowing costs only form part of the Councils revenue budget once the project has been completed, so although there may be a borrowing requirement, until such time as the project is complete there will be no MRP or interest payable as part of the revenue budget.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-15"},"name":"West Suffolk","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":false,"headline":"Overall borrowing expected to increase over the year despite early external debt repayment","lead":"Signals ongoing cash management pressure; the substantial internal borrowing (\u00a360.6m) and expected overall increase warrant monitoring for potential future PWLB drawdown","also":["1 other finding in this window"],"watch":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee on 2026-09-24","n_findings":2,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"CAB-WS-26-039-Recs-from-PASC-Treasury-Management-Report-June-2026","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59409/59409.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":61,"news_drafts_total":3}}